  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health regions with a Regional Pandemic, Epidemic and Health Emergency  Response Plan adopted by the Ministry of Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="0.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="95.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;In 2023, the Ministry of Health (&lt;em&amp;gt;Secretar&amp;iacute;a de Salud&lt;/em&amp;gt;, SESAL) developed and adopted Regional Pandemic, Epidemic, and Health Emergency Response Plans (&lt;em&amp;gt;Planes Regionales de Respuesta a Emergencias para las Regiones Sanitarias&lt;/em&amp;gt;) in the 20 Health Regions in Honduras, thus this indicator is 100% achieved. Regional Emergency Plans provided a robust framework for Government response during the COVID-19 pandemic. Additionally, SESAL updated the multi-threat plan for emergencies and disasters in the healt sector 2022-2023, which establishes a national, intersectoral and inter-institutional response framework to strengthen the sector&amp;#39;s response capacity in emergencies.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="100.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">New or updated Sistema Nacional de Gestin de Riesgos (SINAGER) DRM instruments formulated and approved by the new Ministry of Disaster Risk Management and National Contingencies (COPECO)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="0.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;COPECO formulated and approved the new SINAGER Law as part of its continuous efforts to strengthen the national legal framework for DRM. In May 2022, the new SINAGER Law was submitted to Congress for approval. Although the Law&amp;rsquo;s formulation and approval by COPECO is attributable as a valid target, the Law was pending Congress approval at Project closing. This presents a significant risk to sustainability of development outcomes, as detailed in Section V. COPECO adapted and approved the Index for Risk Management (INFORM), an internationally recognized tool that assesses the risk of humanitarian crises and disasters that may exceed the response capacity of a country, at the municipal level and developed a Geographic Information System (GIS) platform called the &lt;em&amp;gt;Geoportal de Riesgos de COPECO, &lt;/em&amp;gt;which serves as a centralized repository for all digital cartographic information available in the county. With these three instruments the result indicator was 100% achieved.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="3.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water Basin Councils created and operating to reduce waterrelated risks, in the Dry Corridor region in line with the Water Security Strategy</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="0.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="5.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;SERNA formed and trained four (out of five) Sub-Basin Councils in the Dry Corridor region, corresponding to Nacaome, Sampile, Goascor&amp;aacute;n, and the lower Choluteca basins. These were operating to reduce water-related risks, in line with the Water Security Strategy. As a result, the indicator was 80% achieved. The fifth council was in process of being created, however it was not achieved by Project closing.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="4.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Weekly epidemiological reports of mandatory notifiable conditions, produced and disseminated following international standards</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="0.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="52.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;SESAL continued to produce and disseminate weekly epidemiological reports, adhering to established international standards for mandatory notification, thereby achieving 100% compliance with this indicator. These reports served as a valuable resource for monitoring and analyzing public health trends. SESAL published these reports on its official website, making them readily available to the public for easy access and reference.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="52.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">New financial instruments  implemented to manage disaster risk and  emergencies in accordance with the Disaster Risk  Financing Strategy</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="0.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="1.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;SEFIN reported it developed a total of seven financial instruments under the DRFS: (i) national and external budget reallocations to support emergencies; (ii) the activation of the CERC (Contingency Emergency Response Component) to support the response to COVID-19, as well as reallocation of other external funds to support response efforts; (iii) external investment projects for the recovery to Eta and Iota (including WB operation); (iv) a contingent line of credit from the WB; (v) non reimbursable cooperation; (vi) placement of bonds in the national market; and (vii) a contingent line of credit from Inter- American Development Bank. Of the financial instruments reported by SEFIN, number (iv) refers to the contingent line of credit obtained through this Cat DDO and is not attributable as a valid target. Therefore, SEFIN delivered six financial instruments out of one established as a target, thus this indicator was 100% achieved.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="6.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Municipalities that have formulated or updated and formally approved their local emergency plans in accordance with the new operational guidelines</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2020-04-29" value="6.00" year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-04-29"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="40.00">
      <comment>
